<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Shakespeare returns two weeks after his first visit. He saw Dr. Osei-Carrow of movement disorders neurology this morning. Since the brief intervention he has had about 14 standard drinks a week, no more than four on any day, down from about 24; he notices that his hand is worst the morning after an evening of drinking and steadier for an hour after a glass of wine. He has had no sweats, anxiety, or craving on the lighter weeks. He has cut coffee to three cups a day. He brought a page of his handwriting from ten years ago and one written this morning: the recent script is larger, jagged, and drifts upward at the line ends. He has no slowness, stiffness, shuffling, change in his voice or face, loss of smell, constipation, or acting out of dreams. He takes no medicines. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Tremor</td><td>Both hands, right worse, when writing, holding a cup, or pouring; not at rest</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>About 14 drinks a week since the brief intervention, from about 24; a drink steadies the hand for an hour</td></tr><tr><td>Caffeine</td><td>Down to three cups of coffee a day</td></tr><tr><td>Handwriting</td><td>Larger, jagged, drifting script compared with a sample from ten years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Parkinsonian symptoms</td><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

